Five Chain-of-Density iterations complete. The final pass holds roughly 80 words and has absorbed nine added entities across the rounds, including the three-part audit, the durable-capture destinations (ledger, issue, plan, note), the amend-at-HEAD versus buried-commit handling, the bare-dot approval prompt, and the silence rule.

<RESULT>
After plan execution in idle sessions, a checkup (self-decide whether to act) audits three things: planned tasks done and marked, execution-surfaced ideas captured durably (ledger, issue, plan, note), work committed and pushed naming closed issues. Amend an unpushed closing commit at HEAD so pushes carry record; one buried under later commits gets issues named in next commit's message. Act on failures; push when segments complete, else brief reasons; approval-needing items await bare-dot prompts; silence when clean, answering as if absent.
</RESULT>
